{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":29346991,"ns":0,"title":"Science of science policy","extract":"Science of science policy (SoSP) is an emerging interdisciplinary research area that seeks to develop theoretical and empirical models of the scientific enterprise. This scientific basis can be used to help government, and society in general, make better R&D management decisions by establishing a scientifically rigorous, quantitative basis from which policy makers and researchers may assess the impacts of the nation's scientific and engineering enterprise, improve their understanding of its dynamics, and assess the likely outcomes.","description":"Interdisciplinary research area","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}